      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McCormack Quinn are delighted to announce this fabulous property Laurel Lodge, Kildavin, Murrintown, Co. Wexford to the market.\n\nThis impressive detached residence enjoys a wonderful sense of privacy and retreat, while offering exceptionally spacious and well balanced accommodation extending to approximately 210 sq.m.\n\nFrom the moment you arrive, the property's mature setting creates an immediate sense of arrival. Internally, the home has been thoughtfully designed to combine comfortable family living with elegant entertaining spaces, resulting in a residence that is both practical and inviting.\n\nAt the heart of the home lies a beautifully appointed kitchen, finished with sleek contemporary cabinetry, quality work surfaces, a central island and an abundance of natural light. The kitchen flows effortlessly into a dining and entertaining area, creating a welcoming hub for everyday family life and social gatherings alike.\nThe property benefits from two distinctive reception rooms. A stunning sunroom style living space is flooded with natural light through extensive glazing and enjoys uninterrupted views of the gardens, while a second reception room offers a warm and cosy atmosphere, perfect for relaxing evenings by the fire.\n\nThe four generously proportioned bedrooms are bright, spacious, and ideally suited to family living, guest accommodation, or home office use. There are two well appointed bathrooms, while a practical utility room incorporates an additional guest w.c. adding further convenience to the ground floor accommodation.\n\nOne of the property's most outstanding features is its exceptional outdoor space. The substantial rear garden provides a private haven for families and outdoor entertaining, offering ample room for children to play, al fresco dining, gardening enthusiasts, or future landscaping opportunities. Combined with the privacy afforded by the sweeping driveway, the grounds create a setting that is both tranquil and highly desirable. The detached garage features an electric roller door with fitted P.V Solar Panels.\n\nLocated just outside the popular Village of Murrintown, within easy walking distance of Village amenities including mini market, pub, post office, church and primary school to name but a few. Wexford Town Centre with its abundance of shops, supermarkets and main shopping thoroughfare is just a 10 minute drive away. \n\nBlending generous proportions, versatile living space, and a wonderful sense of privacy, this is a home that offers the perfect balance of comfort, style, and practicality for modern family living.\n\nVirtual tour online."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 3.8 x 2.3m\nOpening and welcoming entrance hall that invites you into the home with high ceilings, solid wood flooring.\n\nLiving Room - 5.36 x 4.14m\nLiving room that is spacious and engulfed in natural lighting and seamlessly flows into the sun room, feature marble fireplace, solid wood flooring.\n\nSunroom - 3.76m x 3.26m\nSunroom that is filled with natural light and gives stunning views of the landscape of the property, door to rear garden onto the patio.\n\nKitchen/ Dining - 6.32m x 5.14m\nModernised kitchen/dining room, fully fitted kitchen, feature island unit, tile splashback, recessed lighting, tiled floor.\n\nUtility Room - 3.91m x 2.43m\nFully plumbed, fitted waist to eye level units, access to rear garden, tiled floor.\n\nToilet - \nUtility complimented with w.c., w.h.b.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.63m x 4.03m\nFeature bay window, solid wood flooring.\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 2.43m x 1.92m\nFully tiled with w.c., w.h.b. and electric shower unit.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nLanding - 5.14m x 3.47m\nCarpet to floor.\n\nBedroom 2 - 5.14m x 3.43m\nBright spacious second bedroom, carpet to floor.\n\nBedroom 3 - 5.71m x 2.53m\nBright spacious third bedroom, carpet to floor.\n\nBathroom - 3.55m x 2.25m\nFully tiled with w.c., w.h.b., corner jacuzzi bath and separate shower.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.97m x 3.87m\nFeature bay window, bright spacious fourth bedroom, capet to floor.\n\n"
